263
00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.778
Multipart: initiate returns an upload id.

264
00:14:16.058 --> 00:14:24.954
Parts (5 MB, 5 GB on S3; VERIFY limits for your store) are uploaded independently, in parallel, and retried alone.

265
00:14:25.234 --> 00:14:32.786
Each part has a checksum. complete assembles them atomically. abort or lifecycle rules clean up abandoned uploads.

266
00:14:34.136 --> 00:14:40.557
Pre-signed URLs: the app authorises the upload and hands the client URLs for direct PUTs.

267
00:14:40.837 --> 00:14:43.419
The bytes never pass through application servers.

268
00:14:43.699 --> 00:14:48.029
Scope them tightly (key, size, content type, a few minutes' expiry).

269
00:14:48.309 --> 00:15:00.192
Resumable uploads: persist the upload id and completed parts on the client, and continue after an app restart or a network change (tus protocol or the store's native API).

270
00:15:00.472 --> 00:15:03.715
Integrity: per-part checksums and an end-to-end checksum.

271
00:15:03.995 --> 00:15:05.936
Reject anything that doesn't match.

272
00:15:07.286 --> 00:15:11.894
Parallelism helps until the link or the per-prefix request rate is the limit.

273
00:15:12.174 --> 00:15:13.987
