353
00:18:20.269 --> 00:18:26.989
Eager versus lazy: on a busy catalogue nearly every variant is requested anyway (97%).

354
00:18:27.269 --> 00:18:32.261
Lazy wins for sparse catalogues and for new sizes, because there is no backfill.

355
00:18:32.541 --> 00:18:47.239
Common design: an on-the-fly transform service behind the CDN (URL like or img/id/hash/w300.webp), results cached in the object store, and the top sizes made eagerly.

356
00:18:47.519 --> 00:18:54.453
